From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: gs101: wait 500 ms per relink try

Now and then the s5123 endpoint is not detected yet when a relink try
starts; 150 ms per try was too short and a run of failed tries crashed the
CP (2026-10-09). Local.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs101.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs101.c
@@ -79,12 +79,14 @@
 #define to_gs101_pcie(x)	dev_get_drvdata((x)->dev)
 
 /*
- * exynos_pcie_poweron() link training: tries and wait per try. The vendor
- * retries up to 10 times with ~24-48 ms each; a good relink here reaches L0
- * well inside 150 ms, and 5 tries stay inside the CP's ~3 s wakeup budget.
+ * exynos_pcie_poweron() link training: tries and wait per try. Training
+ * itself takes ~25 ms, but now and then the endpoint is not detected yet
+ * (LTSSM stays in Detect) when a try starts; give each try 500 ms before
+ * re-asserting PERST# and starting over (was 150 ms x 5: a run of those
+ * failures ended with the CP dropping PHONE_ACTIVE, 2026-10-09).
  */
-#define GS101_RELINK_TRIES	5
-#define GS101_RELINK_WAIT_MS	150
+#define GS101_RELINK_TRIES	4
+#define GS101_RELINK_WAIT_MS	500
 
 /*
  * The Samsung CP interface driver addresses root complexes by channel number
